The leave-type option labels are built with `label: leaveType`, using the raw English `CONST.CHRONOS.OOO_LEAVE_TYPES` values (`'parental leave'`, `'maternity leave'`, `'jury duty'`, etc.) directly as user-visible text. These labels render in the `ValueSelectorModal` list and as the `MenuItemWithTopDescription` title, so they will always appear in English regardless of the user's locale. Note the `NORMAL` entry is correctly localized via `translate('chronos.normalOOO')`, but the rest are not.

Add a translation key for each leave type (e.g. `chronos.parentalLeave`, `chronos.maternityLeave`, …) to every `src/languages/*` file and map each value to its translated label:

```tsx
const leaveTypeLabels = {
    [CONST.CHRONOS.OOO_LEAVE_TYPES.NORMAL]: translate('chronos.normalOOO'),
    [CONST.CHRONOS.OOO_LEAVE_TYPES.PARENTAL]: translate('chronos.parentalLeave'),
    // …one entry per leave type
};
const leaveTypeItems = Object.values(CONST.CHRONOS.OOO_LEAVE_TYPES).map((leaveType) => ({value: leaveType, label: leaveTypeLabels[leaveType]}));
```

The cash back badge text `'Cash back'` is a hardcoded, user-visible string. Every other branch in this same `getSettlementStatusBadgeProps` function renders its badge text through `translate('settlement.status.*')`, so this new branch is the only one that will not localize and will always display English.

Add a translation key (e.g. `settlement.status.cashBack: 'Cash back'` in `src/languages/*`) and render it via the `translate` param that is already passed into this function:

```ts
if (isCashbackCredit) {
    return {
        text: translate('settlement.status.cashBack'),
        badgeStyles: {
            backgroundColor: theme.reportStatusBadge.paid.backgroundColor,
        },
        textStyles: {
            color: theme.reportStatusBadge.paid.textColor,
        },
    };
}
```

The `accessibilityLabel="Edit cell"` is a hardcoded user-facing string. Accessibility labels are surfaced to screen-reader users, so they must be localized via the translation method rather than hardcoded in English, otherwise the label cannot be translated for non-English users.

Add a translation entry (e.g. `common.edit` or a dedicated key) to `src/languages/*` and pull it through `useLocalize`:

```tsx
const {translate} = useLocalize();
// ...
<PressableWithFeedback
    accessibilityRole={CONST.ROLE.BUTTON}
    accessibilityLabel={translate('common.edit')}
    sentryLabel={CONST.SENTRY_LABEL.TABLE.EDITABLE_CELL}
    // ...
>
```
